
LIB 7 "DPMI Programming", BcppDOS file descriptions.


!LONG!


LIB 7

[76424,2231]    Lib:7
16MOUS.ZIP/Bin  Bytes:   1566, Count:   57, 25-Jul-94

  Title   : Simulate real mode interrupt example
  Keywords: DPMI 16 MOUSE SIMULATE REAL MODE INTERRUPT

  Example of how to call DPMI function 300h (simulate real mode
  interrupt). This example calls mouse interrupt 0x33, function 9, to change
  the  graphics cursor.

[76424,2231]    Lib:7
SLFMOD.ZIP/Bin  Bytes:    896, Count:   56, 25-Jul-94

  Title   : 32-bit DPMI self modifying code example
  Keywords: SELF MODIFYING CODE 32 DPMI

  Self modifying code example for 32-bit DPMI

[76030,303]     Lib:7
INT32.ZIP/Bin   Bytes:   5598, Count:   80, 24-Jul-94

  Title   : 32bit interrupt thunk code
  Keywords: INTERRUPT 32BIT POWERPAK POWERPACK

  Library and source code to allow developers to use 16bit style
  C/C++ interrupt functions in 32bit mode.  See README for complete
  details. Library is pre-built, but requires assembler to be rebuilt.

[76702,1063]    Lib:7
LINEAR.ZIP/Bin  Bytes:   2208, Count:  102, 23-Jul-94

  Title   : Access DPMI32 video memory from DS (no selectors)
  Keywords: DPMI DPMI32 LINEAR ADDRESS

  Example of how to call DPMI functions to map physical memory ranges
  into your DPMI32 process address space.  This allows you to access video
  (text or graphics) memory via an offset into your DS.  IOW no selector
  loads.

[70152,3410]    Lib:7
SWLM32.C/Text   Bytes:   4451, Count:  118, 15-Jul-94

  Title   : Improved lowmem32.c pgm
  Keywords: DPMI DOS32 DOS LOW POWERPACK SCREEN BIOS ASM 1M

  This file is an improved version of Borland's lowmem32.c example. Use this
  file to access memory below 1M using PowerPack's DOS 32 extender. Using
  Borland's DOS 32 extender, you cannot directly access low memory using C
  pointers. This routine uses asm to get/set low memory. Improvements are:
  faster get/set operations using 8, 16, and 32 operations. You don't have to
  use offset and selector parameters - only a C pointer. Also, you can use
  either low or high mem address values, works with either.

